---
source: tests/help_snapshot.rs
expression: "help(&[\"disasm\", \"--help\"])"
---
Disassemble code

Usage: gd disasm [OPTIONS] [TARGET]

Arguments:
  [TARGET]  Target (name | 0xaddr | FUN_<hex>)

Options:
      --target <TARGET>
          Target (name | 0xaddr | FUN_<hex>)
  -n, --instructions <NUM_INSTRUCTIONS>
          Number of instructions to disassemble
      --end <END>
          Disassemble until this address (range mode; use instead of -n)
      --no-resolve
          Do not resolve literal pool loads (faster, no `loaded` fields)
      --program <PROGRAM>
          
      --project <PROJECT>
          
  -f, --filter <FILTER>
          Filter expression: <field><op><value>, e.g. 'name~PK' (contains), 'name=~"^PK_"' (regex), 'size>100'. Ops: = != > >= < <= ~ ^ $ =~. Combine with AND/OR/NOT. Bare words are rejected
      --fields <FIELDS>
          
  -o, --format <FORMAT>
          
      --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of results (0 = unlimited; default 1000)
      --offset <OFFSET>
          
      --sort <SORT>
          
      --count
          
      --json
          
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity printed to stdout (-v=warn, -vv=info, -vvv=debug)
  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output
      --pretty
          Output JSON with pretty formatting
      --projects-dir <PROJECTS_DIR>
          Directory under which Ghidra projects are stored. Overrides config `ghidra_project_dir` and the default location. Note: Ghidra 12.1+ rejects paths containing a dot-prefixed component
      --java-home <JAVA_HOME>
          Full JDK home for Ghidra to use (must be a JDK, not a JRE). Overrides config `java_home` and auto-detection
  -h, --help
          Print help
